{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1166312-reflavoring-mechanics","id":1166312,"title":"Reflavoring Mechanics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-09T11:22:09-08:00","id":1166312,"title":"Reflavoring Mechanics","content":"Getting the most out of the mechanics: Different ways to flavor your Beast's powers. An important thing to remember when thinking of new ways to flavor your Atavisms is that they can also represent aspects of your lair; your Beast's Dragonfire could just as easily be him calling up the searing flames of his lair rather than having literal fiery breath. Remember also that Beast powers don't have to obey physical laws and can exploit bizarre dream logic. Note that none of these flavor changes can alter mechanics or give a system advantage. I have a few here that i've come up with, feel free to add your own ideas.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>ATAVISMS</b><br /> Basilisk's Touch: A poisonous melee attack. Too easy to think of ways you can represent this.<br /> Poisoned Blood - The Horror seeps its lethal blood on things it touches. Also works with drugs and plague-carrying Horrors.<br /> Venomous Lair - The beast has some toxic substance in its lair, which it calls forth with a touch.<br /> <br /> Infestation: A seemingly-niche Atavism, infestation can be reflavored in a number of creative ways to fit most any Beast's needs.<br /> Small toys - a collection of small plastic toys (which, disturbingly, still bleed and go squish)<br /> Tiny monsters - Minute, terrifying supernatural creatures. Many Beasts can pull this one off.<br /> <br /> Limb From Limb: The basic 'Do lots of melee damage' Atavism. So many ways to do this one aside from the usual claws and teeth.<br /> Minions: Deadly creatures from the Horror's Lair or extensions of the Horror leap out and savage victims when the monster attacks.<br /> <br /> Looming Presence: This Atavism represents their effectively being more of the Horror. There's a few ways to flavor this.<br /> Horde/Multitude - Rather than being larger, the Horror is composed of many humanoid or even animal-sized beings.<br /> Unthinkably large - The Horror is so massive that only its extremities are ever even seen. Its limbs, tendrils, etc. are massive and viewing the full being is impossible or undesirable due to its colossal size or mind-bending alien visage.<br /> <br /> Shadowed Soul: A fun Atavism to represent the ever-present threats of many sneaky, stalking monsters.<br /> Slasher Walk - You know those superhuman killers in Slasher flicks who walk super slowly but always seem to keep up with victims running at top speed<br /> and appear out of nowhere right by you? This is how a Beast does that, especially combined with From the Shadows.<br /> Shortcuts - The beast steps into a shadow and calls down a bit of its lair, moving swiftly through a place it knows intimately and emerging elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Unbreakable: The standard 'you can't hurt me' Atavism. So many ways to represent this.<br /> Tough, thick skin - the obvious one. From a troll's knotty hide to a stone monster's hard exterior or a plant creature's barklike body.<br /> Cartoonish Physiology - Hits deform the beast's body but do no real damage. Works with dream logic or a plastic man sort of monster.<br /> The No Sell - Damage appears to harm the beast, but the monster never bleeds or suffers any harm until damage is actually done to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/11.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":16101,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","user":"Eternal Darkness","date":".  Spelling, grammar and punctuation 12-09-2017, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","name":"Eternal Darkness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-09T13:20:34-08:00","id":1166327,"title":"","content":"I'm all for taking a lot of flavor liberties with Atavisms and how to describe them in a way that matches a Beast's Horror. The book is abundantly clear this is supposed to be the case.<br /> <br /> However, I'm not sure &quot;channeling your Lair&quot; thing is productive because Beasts can already literally do that. If you want to express &quot;fire&quot; in a fashion besides Dragon's Breath, there's options. You can reflavor Limb from Limb to create burns with your physical attacks, or Basilisk's Touch to literally boil their blood, or have Fiery as a Lair Trait and inflict it on the scene.<br /> <br /> But you have to pick the mechanics that match what you're trying to do, or there's going to be dissonance between them and the reflavor. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-09T14:02:57-08:00","id":1166334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1166312-reflavoring-mechanics?p=1166327#post1166327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm all for taking a lot of flavor liberties with Atavisms and how to describe them in a way that matches a Beast's Horror. The book is abundantly clear this is supposed to be the case.<br /> <br /> However, I'm not sure &quot;channeling your Lair&quot; thing is productive because Beasts can already literally do that. If you want to express &quot;fire&quot; in a fashion besides Dragon's Breath, there's options. You can reflavor Limb from Limb to create burns with your physical attacks, or Basilisk's Touch to literally boil their blood, or have Fiery as a Lair Trait and inflict it on the scene.<br /> <br /> But you have to pick the mechanics that match what you're trying to do, or there's going to be dissonance between them and the reflavor.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Beasts can literally do that with at least one Atavism, too: Storm-Lashed. Explicitly stated in its description, and ultimately it doesn't matter how it's described if it changes no mechanics. I also said right in the topic paragraph 'Note that none of these flavor changes can alter mechanics or give a system advantage.'.<br /> <br /> Thanks for your input anyway, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/11.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","name":"Eternal Darkness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T08:07:21-08:00","id":1167305,"title":"","content":"I think the trouble with Venomous as an Atavism is, that it is already covered by the Toxic Lair Trait, although I AM a big fan of spores, miasma and similar monstrous abilities. And as you rightly pointed out, the divide is not as clear-cut as we sometimes like to belief, so let's just go with what's fun.<br /> <br /> I like to interpret Infestation differently for some Beasts, for example: instead of being a multitude of insects, the Beast is living liquid - e.g. Water elemental or T2000's mercurial form.<br /> <br /> I also like the Monster From The Deep as actual Mind-Over-Matter to represent the reach increase, or having the attacks be telekinetic blows that do not need to connect as long as they come somewhat close, or have a simple fling with Limb From Limb have the same impact as a powerful punch.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T21:18:16-08:00","id":1168114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1166312-reflavoring-mechanics?p=1167305#post1167305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the trouble with Venomous as an Atavism is, that it is already covered by the Toxic Lair Trait, although I AM a big fan of spores, miasma and similar monstrous abilities. And as you rightly pointed out, the divide is not as clear-cut as we sometimes like to belief, so let's just go with what's fun.<br /> <br /> I like to interpret Infestation differently for some Beasts, for example: instead of being a multitude of insects, the Beast is living liquid - e.g. Water elemental or T2000's mercurial form.<br /> <br /> I also like the Monster From The Deep as actual Mind-Over-Matter to represent the reach increase, or having the attacks be telekinetic blows that do not need to connect as long as they come somewhat close, or have a simple fling with Limb From Limb have the same impact as a powerful punch.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That infestation one is brilliant and i am using it for an amoeba-like primordial ooze Horror some day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/11.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","name":"Eternal Darkness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T12:39:56-08:00","id":1168235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eternal Darkness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1166312-reflavoring-mechanics?p=1168114#post1168114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That infestation one is brilliant and i am using it for an amoeba-like primordial ooze Horror some day.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm doing that, too. His Lair is a series of tunnels, and as he advances, his increasing number of Lair Traits will all reflect the tunnels gradually filling with acidic slime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T10:53:35-08:00","id":1168562,"title":"","content":"glad you like the idea.<br /> Anyone got any cool ideas on how to reflavour Storm-Lashed? I was thinking water-based. Rain and gushes of water, maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T11:18:38-08:00","id":1168571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1166312-reflavoring-mechanics?p=1168562#post1168562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">glad you like the idea.<br /> Anyone got any cool ideas on how to reflavour Storm-Lashed? I was thinking water-based. Rain and gushes of water, maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>That works. Again, a case could be made for telekinesis, as well as gravitic manipulation. That could work for Wings of the Raptor as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T06:13:25-08:00","id":1169066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1166312-reflavoring-mechanics?p=1168571#post1168571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That works. Again, a case could be made for telekinesis, as well as gravitic manipulation. That could work for Wings of the Raptor as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point.<br /> Also, I want to point to Heart of the Ocean being easily reshaped into something like Heart of the Desert, to represent tremor-worms and stuff, and bestow the ability to &quot;swim&quot; in sand. We did that in the homebrew folder, somewhere, I am sure.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T06:46:11-08:00","id":1169071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1166312-reflavoring-mechanics?p=1169066#post1169066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good point.<br /> Also, I want to point to Heart of the Ocean being easily reshaped into something like Heart of the Desert, to represent tremor-worms and stuff, and bestow the ability to &quot;swim&quot; in sand. We did that in the homebrew folder, somewhere, I am sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>We called it 'The Maggot God'.<br /> <br /> Re: reskinning Dragonfire, Cinder did an excellent water-type reskinning in his Beast Dark Era, The Forest that Weeps:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Breath of the River</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>:</b> Breath of the River is a modified version of Dragonfire. Instead of torrents of flames, a Beast with Breath of the River is able to unleash high-pressured jets of water from her mouth, either in the shape of destructive projectiles or geysers of terrifying strength. It works as Dragonfire unless specified, except it does not grant immunity to fire and smoke and obviously cannot be used to burn materials or set places alight (putting out fires, on the other hand\u2026). The other differences are: </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Normal Effect</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Beast can breath underwater and can see in the dark and through the murkiest waters, suffering no environmental penalties. While Beasts with this Atavism gain the ability to breathe underwater, they must take an instant action to give their lungs time to adjust when switching atmospheres.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> Damage against living beings is considered Lethal instead of Aggravate, but those hit by the water are subjected to the Drowning Tilt for a number of turns equal to the Beast\u2019s Lair. Breath of the River ignores the same amount of Durability Dragonfire would.</span></span><br /> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T07:29:54-08:00","id":1169078,"title":"","content":"Huh. I have to admit I dislike that this has a LOT of crossing over with Heart of the Ocean while also providing an attack. I'd rather see something like &quot;Can discharge toxins from its body by violently vomiting them out in an instant action. This can double as an attack, but with reduced range&quot;.<br /> I DO very much like the Sat Expend.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T07:31:04-08:00","id":1169079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1166312-reflavoring-mechanics?p=1169071#post1169071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We called it 'The Maggot God'.<br /> <br /> Re: reskinning Dragonfire, Cinder did an excellent water-type reskinning in his Beast Dark Era, The Forest that Weeps:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for mentioning me, Ajf. Reflavoring Atavisms and Nightmares is one of the most fun parts of Beast, I think I have made dozens of these, for a reason or another<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1166312-reflavoring-mechanics?p=1169078#post1169078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. I have to admit I dislike that this has a LOT of crossing over with Heart of the Ocean while also providing an attack. I'd rather see something like &quot;Can discharge toxins from its body by violently vomiting them out in an instant action. This can double as an attack, but with reduced range&quot;.<br /> I DO very much like the Sat Expend.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does, but it was made for a specific character in mind and fit the picture. I don't like that part much either, but other options did not fit at all. Context improves it a little, but your point is 100% fair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 12-20-2017, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T07:31:56-08:00","id":1169080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1166312-reflavoring-mechanics?p=1169079#post1169079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for mentioning me, Ajf. Reflavoring Atavisms and Nightmares is one of the most fun parts of Beast, I think I have made dozens of these, for a reason or another</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you be willing to collate them here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T07:41:06-08:00","id":1169083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1166312-reflavoring-mechanics?p=1169080#post1169080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you be willing to collate them here?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, most are just basic alterations like that one. Think I made all kinds of Dragonfire, from the classics to weirder ones like a Fallout-esque nuclear waste or glass, for example.<br /> <br /> I'll need to write them properly in order to present them to the civilized society but sure, I'll see what I can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 12-20-2017, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T07:44:51-08:00","id":1169084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1166312-reflavoring-mechanics?p=1169083#post1169083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, most are just basic alterations like that one. Think I made all kinds of Dragonfire, from the classics to weirder ones like a Fallout-esque nuclear waste or glass, for example.<br /> <br /> I'll need to write them properly in order in order to present them to the civilized society but sure, I'll see what I can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks very much. We appreciate it. Well, I do. I presume these others do as well. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T06:08:52-08:00","id":1171214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1166312-reflavoring-mechanics?p=1169079#post1169079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does, but it was made for a specific character in mind and fit the picture. I don't like that part much either, but other options did not fit at all. Context improves it a little, but your point is 100% fair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, thanks for the answer. I totally understand that something that looks unimpressive, weird or even bad on it's own can be awesome in the right context, so I am thankful for that information (very much a fan of tailored Atavisms), and I just wanted to let you know that.<br /> The opposite is true, too, of course, some things are awesome, but simply might not fit into your Chronicle/Group/Setting/Flow etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> Would like to see more of your other Reflavourings, so seconding ajf115 here.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T12:48:52-08:00","id":1171307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1166312-reflavoring-mechanics?p=1171214#post1171214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey, thanks for the answer. I totally understand that something that looks unimpressive, weird or even bad on it's own can be awesome in the right context, so I am thankful for that information (very much a fan of tailored Atavisms), and I just wanted to let you know that.<br /> The opposite is true, too, of course, some things are awesome, but simply might not fit into your Chronicle/Group/Setting/Flow etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> Would like to see more of your other Reflavourings, so seconding ajf115 here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't mention it, it was the least I could do.<br /> <br /> I'm myself a big proponent for each Beast having a tailored Atavism or two to fit its Legend, either at the beginning or as something gained or evolved later (with the Storyteller's approval, of course) by justifying it in game as the Beast's myth growing and changing.<br /> <br /> I've added writing all those down on the list of the things to do. Might take a while since I've plenty of work to do either here, on my blog or elsewhere and some of those things have a deadline, but I'll get to it. Thanks for the trust shown about how they might turn out.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, I realize it might not be the same considering the less than serious context, but I just made three of those in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1170442-christmas-bonus-klaus-krampus\">this thread</a>, if you're interested","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 12-28-2017, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}